Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."trip_id": unique identifier we need to output  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."duration_sec": used for ranking the longest trips  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."start_date": filter trips between 2017‑07‑01 and 2017‑12‑31  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."start_station_name": needed in result, also used to build route  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."end_station_name": combine with start station to make route text  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."start_station_id": join key to station information table  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."bike_number": show in result  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."subscriber_type": show in result  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."member_birth_year": calculate member’s current age  
• BIKESHARE_TRIPS."member_gender": show in result, also used for filtering non‑null rows  
• BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO."station_id": join key that matches start_station_id  
• BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO."region_id": tells which region a station belongs to  
• BIKESHARE_REGIONS."region_id": join key to get text name of region  
• BIKESHARE_REGIONS."name": final region name we need  
Conditions that will be applied later  
1.  start_date  between 2017‑07‑01 00:00:00 and 2017‑12‑31 23:59:59 (after converting the micro‑second epoch to TIMESTAMP)  
2.  "start_station_name", "member_birth_year" and "member_gender" IS NOT NULL  
3.  order by "duration_sec" DESC and LIMIT 5  

Ten exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries  
```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at raw trip rows
SELECT *
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect distinct start station names that are not null
SELECT DISTINCT "start_station_name"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS"
WHERE "start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Inspect station info records to see region_id values
SELECT "station_id",
       "name",
       "region_id"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Check region dictionary table
SELECT *
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_REGIONS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Join one trip with its station to verify region linkage
SELECT t."trip_id",
       t."start_station_id",
       s."region_id",
       r."name" AS "region_name"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS"  t
LEFT JOIN "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO" s
       ON t."start_station_id" = s."station_id"
LEFT JOIN "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_REGIONS" r
       ON s."region_id" = r."region_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Convert micro‑second epoch to date to make sure filter works
SELECT t."trip_id",
       TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ(t."start_date"/1000000) AS "start_ts"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS" t
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Trips in requested time window (July‑Dec 2017) with non‑null essentials
SELECT t."trip_id",
       t."start_station_name",
       t."member_birth_year",
       t."member_gender",
       TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ(t."start_date"/1000000) AS "start_ts"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS" t
WHERE TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ(t."start_date"/1000000) BETWEEN '2017‑07‑01' AND '2017‑12‑31 23:59:59'
  AND t."start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_gender" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Compute current age for those rows
SELECT t."trip_id",
       DATE_PART('year', CURRENT_DATE) - t."member_birth_year"            AS "age",
       t."member_birth_year"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS" t
WHERE t."member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Produce age class buckets
SELECT t."trip_id",
       CASE
           WHEN (DATE_PART('year', CURRENT_DATE) - t."member_birth_year") < 40 THEN 'Young (<40 Y.O)'
           WHEN (DATE_PART('year', CURRENT_DATE) - t."member_birth_year") BETWEEN 40 AND 60 THEN 'Adult (40‑60 Y.O)'
           ELSE 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)'
       END AS "age_class"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS" t
WHERE t."member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – top 5 longest trips between 2017‑07‑01 and 2017‑12‑31 with all requested fields
SELECT
       t."trip_id",
       t."duration_sec",
       TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ(t."start_date"/1000000)                                 AS "start_timestamp",
       t."start_station_name",
       t."start_station_name" || ' - ' || t."end_station_name"                  AS "route",
       t."bike_number",
       t."subscriber_type",
       t."member_birth_year",
       DATE_PART('year', CURRENT_DATE) - t."member_birth_year"                  AS "current_age",
       CASE
           WHEN (DATE_PART('year', CURRENT_DATE) - t."member_birth_year") < 40          THEN 'Young (<40 Y.O)'
           WHEN (DATE_PART('year', CURRENT_DATE) - t."member_birth_year") BETWEEN 40 AND 60 THEN 'Adult (40‑60 Y.O)'
           ELSE 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)'
       END AS "age_class",
       t."member_gender",
       r."name"                                                                  AS "region_name"
FROM "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_TRIPS"         t
JOIN "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO"  s
     ON t."start_station_id" = s."station_id"
LEFT JOIN "SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS"."SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE"."BIKESHARE_REGIONS"  r
     ON s."region_id" = r."region_id"
WHERE TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ(t."start_date"/1000000) BETWEEN '2017‑07‑01' AND '2017‑12‑31 23:59:59'
  AND t."start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_gender" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY t."duration_sec" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```
